A running server and a recovery record solve different problems. Choose what must survive termination and how the next worker finds it.

> Remember from chapters 8 and 9 that processes lose their state on termination.

Source: [Q02](/lore/durability-bibliography#q02); [B2](/lore/durability-bibliography#b2-elixir-in-action), [B3](/lore/durability-bibliography#b3-designing-elixir-systems-with-otp).

## Failure it prevents

The [service](/lore/services-capture-dependencies) restarts successfully while accepted work disappears.

## Our Effect 4.0.0 reading

`Workflow`, `Activity`, and `WorkflowEngine` describe resumable work. Choose persistent engine storage. `WorkflowEngine.layerMemory` keeps state only in memory.

Source: `packages/effect/src/workflow/Workflow.ts`, `packages/effect/src/workflow/Activity.ts`, `packages/effect/src/workflow/WorkflowEngine.ts`.

## How to check

Kill the worker after acceptance. Recover the same operation identity from the selected backend. This check is our proposal. The books do not prescribe it.

Continue with [Every task needs an owner](/lore/every-task-needs-an-owner), [Checkpoints follow the promised commit](/lore/checkpoints-follow-commits).

Connect this to [the existing rat-stack guidance](/lore/concurrent-work-needs-an-owner).

Use [the durability skill](/skills/durability) for the full review. Return to [the durability index](/lore/durability).
